# Where the Apex Legends weapon catalog comes from

Everything here was read on **2026-10-01**, during **Season 30: Marked, Split 2**
(Season 30 launched 2026-08-04; Split 2 started 2026-09-15); the pictures,
the rarity tiers and the list check were added on **2026-10-21** (still Split
2: EA's news page has no newer patch notes). `catalog.json` in
this folder is every gun a player can pick up in Apex Legends' Battle Royale;
this file says where every fact and every picture in it came from.

**Pictures: publisher pictures only (decision D116).** Every picture in
`weapons/` is Electronic Arts' own image, of two kinds:

- **Locker render** (8 guns, 2026-10-01): cut from the eight screenshots of the
  game's **Legend Locker weapon screen** on EA's own help site (help.ea.com,
  "Apex Legends guns and weapons guide"): the game's own colour weapon
  render, on that screen's blue backdrop.
- **HUD icon** (19 guns, 2026-10-21): the game's own white weapon silhouette,
  the one its HUD and menus draw, cut from the charts Respawn publishes in its
  **Designer's Notes** on ea.com (images on EA's `drop-assets.ea.com`). Each
  chart plots every gun as its icon on a black backdrop. The icons are small
  (about 100 to 210 px wide, as the chart draws them; not enlarged). Axis lines
  and the chart's text labels next to an icon were painted over with the
  backdrop colour; nothing of the gun was changed.

None came from a fan wiki, Fandom, wiki.gg, a loadout site or an image search. They are EA's copyright, used in the app to identify the weapon,
the same risk the owner accepted in D116. Delete a `.png` and set that
weapon's `image` to `null` and the app shows the class symbol instead; nothing
else changes.

## The list

EA's help article **"Apex Legends guns and weapons guide"**
(<https://help.ea.com/en/articles/apex-legends/guns-and-weapons/>, "Updated 2
days ago" when read on 2026-10-01) names every gun class and every gun in it.
Its classes and their order are the game's own: the same as the tabs of the
Legend Locker weapon screen in its screenshots (HAVOC, FLATLINE, HEMLOK, R-301,
NEMESIS for the assault rifles, and so on). The catalog keeps that order.

Counts: **29 guns in 7 classes**: Assault Rifles 5, SMGs 5, LMGs 4, Marksman 4,
Sniper Rifles 4, Shotguns 4, Pistols 3. **27 have an official picture** (8
Locker renders, 19 HUD icons); 2 do not (below).

**EA confirms the 29 (2026-10-21).** Respawn's **Marked Midseason Designer's
Notes** (<https://www.ea.com/games/apex-legends/apex-legends/news/30-1-designers-notes>,
2026-09-10) chart "Season 30 Change in Share of Downs" lists every "Base
Weapon" in Season 30, and they are exactly these 29: Prowler, CAR, P2020,
Scout, R-301, Spitfire, Flatline, EVA-8, Rampage, HAVOC, Mozambique, Mastiff,
Peacekeeper, Nemesis, Bocek Bow, Longbow, Sentinel, Triple Take, Charge Rifle,
L-STAR, Kraber, Wingman, 30-30 Repeater, Volt, Devotion, Hemlok, Alternator,
RE-45 and R-99. That page is now in every item's `sources`. No gun was added
or removed by EA between 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-21 (EA's news page,
<https://www.ea.com/games/apex-legends/apex-legends/news>, lists nothing newer
than the Marked Midseason patch notes but events).

Three names differ between EA's help article and EA's newer patch notes. The
catalog uses the patch notes' name, keeps the other as an `aliases` word (so
search finds both) and marks the item `uncertain`:

- **Hemlok Breach AR** (help article: "Hemlok Burst AR"). EA's Marked patch
  notes (<https://www.ea.com/games/apex-legends/news/marked-patch-notes>) tune
  the "Hemlok Breach AR" and its Breach Charge. The community wiki says the
  Breach AR took the Burst AR's place in floor loot in Season 28 Split 2
  (2026-03-24).
- **RE-45** (help article: "RE-45 Auto"). The Marked patch notes call it
  "RE-45" and give it an energy stockpile. The community wiki says the
  three-round **RE-45 Burst** (energy ammo) replaced the RE-45 Auto in Season 28
  Split 2. If the owner's screen writes "RE-45 BURST", rename the item (its id
  stays `pistols.re_45`).
- **Bocek Compound Bow** (help article: "Bocek 2.0"). EA's Marked Midseason
  patch notes (<https://www.ea.com/games/apex-legends/news/marked-midseason-patch-notes>,
  2026-09-14) call it "Bocek Compound Bow".

**Not in the list, on purpose:** Legend abilities that shoot (Rampart's Sheila,
which is her Ultimate, not a gun you carry), ordnance (grenades, Arc Stars,
thermites), melee (cosmetic in Apex: every Legend punches), and limited-time
mode weapons.

**Akimbo.** The P2020 and the Mozambique Shotgun can be held two at once
("Akimbo"); EA's help article says they take one weapon slot, so they are one
gun each here, not separate entries.

## Care Package and gold weapons

Care Package (supply drop) guns are the same guns as on the floor, moved there
for a season; they are not separate entries, and nothing in the catalog
records the rotation, because it changes every season and the gun's picture
and id do not. For the record, on 2026-10-01: the Marked patch notes move the
**30-30 Repeater** into the Care Package and return the **G7 Scout** to the
floor; press write-ups of Season 30 name the Care Package guns as the
**Kraber .50-Cal Sniper**, the **L-STAR EMG** and the **30-30 Repeater**
(not confirmed by an EA page). Gold weapons are no longer a rotating set
(Marked patch notes, "Gold Weapon Rotation Removed").

## Rarity (`tiers`, read 2026-10-21, D134)

Apex colours a gun by its loot tier. **EA's own words are colours:** the
Marked patch notes (<https://www.ea.com/games/apex-legends/news/marked-patch-notes>)
say "white tiered loot", "White magazine", "Blue attachments", "Blue
magazine", "Purple is now the max upgrade tier", "Gold Weapons"; EA's
weapons guide (<https://help.ea.com/en/articles/apex-legends/guns-and-weapons/>)
calls Care Package weapons "Mythic-tier weapons". So the tier `name`s are
White, Blue, Purple, Gold and Mythic, the words a player hears; the ids are
the usual rarity words (`common`, `rare`, `epic`, `legendary`, `mythic`),
which the community uses for the same tiers.

- **Gold** in Season 30: any gun can spawn gold (Marked: "Gold Weapon Rotation
  Removed", "Gold Weapons are no longer limited to a smaller set of
  weapons"); a gold gun carries the Accelerator Hop-Up, and gold attachments
  are gone from the loot pool.
- **Mythic** is the Care Package guns' tier (the 30-30 Repeater in Season 30,
  per the Marked notes; the Kraber and L-STAR per press, not an EA page).
  Those are always Mythic; every other gun is White to Gold as found. The
  catalog has no per-gun tier field (`README.md`), so this is recorded here
  only.
- **Corrupted** (Season 30) is an *attachment* rarity ("New High Tier
  Attachment Rarity", red in EA's help-article picture), not a gun's; not a
  tier here.
- **The colours are NOT sampled from an EA image.** No EA page read shows a
  gun's tier colour cleanly (the HUD screenshots found show no weapon slot).
  The hex values are Apex's familiar white, blue, purple, gold and red, for
  the app's chip only; the Core learns each tier's colour from the owner's
  own crops (`RECOGNITION.md`, "Rarity"). Replace them with sampled values
  when an official image turns up.

## Ammo (`ammo`)

The ammo each gun takes, as `light`, `heavy`, `energy`, `shotgun`, `sniper` or
`arrows` (EA's help article names those types). The C.A.R. SMG takes both
heavy and light. From the community wiki's ammo page
(<https://apexlegends.wiki.gg/wiki/Ammo>), checked against EA's Marked patch
notes, whose energy rework lists the energy guns: HAVOC, Nemesis, Devotion,
L-STAR, RE-45, Volt and Triple Take (energy ammo boxes were removed in Season
30; those guns now carry a regenerating stockpile). A gun in the Care Package
uses "Mythic" ammo that comes with it while it is there; its `ammo` is still
its own type.

